From cb293f30cefab0ba18b5fbd1cf02717a41e2e450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:54:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(ui): Machines pane "Use for this setup" assigns the
 selected machine

The Machines pane's detail view gains a "Use for this setup" button. It
queues CommandKind::UseCatalogueMachine, which the state drain turns
into the existing LoadMachine command via the new
LoadMachine::from_catalogue - the same carrier the Setup pane's machine
picker, editor Apply and ribbon machine door use, since the machine is
the document singleton (there is no per-setup machine). Undo restores
the previous machine; redo assigns it again.

from_catalogue re-reads the built-in text or the file and re-validates
it, refusing by the first refusal, so a refused file never mounts even
if queued directly. The pane disables the button with the reason shown
(and as hover text) via MachineEntry::assign_block: a validation
refusal, or the machine already being the setup's.

Decision (docs/decisions/384-machines-use-for-setup.md): the Setup
pane's machine editor window folds into the Machines pane as its edit
mode when the edit slice lands; unchanged here.

Pinned by machine_assign (app) and the machines_pane ui tests.

Fixes #384

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
